ORDER PROCESSING EXPECTED BEHAVIOUR

PRODUCTS AND INVENTORY

1. A product has SKU, name, category, price and weight (kg).
   Categories: electronics (18% tax), clothing (12%), grocery (5%),
   books (0%). Price cannot be negative. Weight must be > 0.

2. Inventory available stock = physical stock - reserved stock.

3. Reserving more than the available stock is an error.

4. Releasing a reservation decreases ONLY the reserved count.
   The units never left the warehouse, so physical stock is unchanged.

5. Committing at shipping decreases BOTH physical and reserved
   stock. Example: stock 10, reserved 3, commit 3 -> stock 7,
   reserved 0, available 7.

CART AND COUPONS

6. Adding the same SKU to a cart again increases its quantity.

7. A percent coupon applies only to eligible categories.
   Example: 10% electronics-only coupon; books 100 + electronics
   100 -> discount is 10, not 20.

8. A fixed coupon is limited to the eligible subtotal.
   A coupon's max_discount, if set, caps the discount.
   A coupon whose min_subtotal is not reached is an error.

PRICING PIPELINE (this order must be followed)

9. Subtotal first, then coupon discount, then tax, then shipping.

10. Tax is charged per line on the amount AFTER that line's share
    of the discount. Example: electronics 100, discount share 10
    -> taxable 90 -> tax 16.2 (not 18.0).

11. The discount is shared across eligible lines in proportion to
    their subtotals. Ineligible lines receive no discount share.

12. Shipping base depends on the DISCOUNTED subtotal:
    500 or more = free, 200-499.99 = 40, below 200 = 60.
    Example: subtotal 550 with 20% coupon -> discounted 440 ->
    base shipping 40 (not free).

13. Weight surcharge: first 5 kg included; each extra kilogram OR
    PART of one (rounded up) costs 30, even if base shipping is free.
    Example: 7.2 kg -> 3 extra units -> surcharge 90.

14. Empty cart: every charge is 0, including shipping.

15. Total = (subtotal - discount) + tax + shipping.
    Money is rounded to two decimal places.

ORDERS

16. Order lifecycle: CREATED -> PLACED -> PAID -> SHIPPED.
    Cancellation is allowed from CREATED, PLACED or PAID only.

17. Placing an order reserves stock ALL-OR-NOTHING.
    Example: stock A=5, B=1; cart needs A=2, B=3 -> placing fails
    and A's available stock is still 5 afterwards.

18. Shipping commits stock. Example: stock 10, order of 3 placed,
    paid and shipped -> stock 7, reserved 0, available 7.

19. Cancelling a placed order restores availability exactly.
    Example: stock 10, order of 3 placed then cancelled ->
    stock 10, reserved 0, available 10 (never 13).

20. Payment freezes the per-unit paid price (after discount,
    including tax) for every line.

21. Returns are allowed only after shipping, never more than was
    purchased. Returned units go back into physical stock.

22. A return refunds the FROZEN paid price per unit, even if the
    product price changed after payment.
    Example: paid 106.2 per unit; price later rises to 150;
    returning 1 unit refunds 106.2 (not 177.0).
